CLASS com/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1395 com/xk72/proxy/ssl/MaybeSSLRecordListener
	COMMENT [inferred] the callback interface SSLRecordParser drives as it walks the TLS record
	COMMENT layer; SSLHandshakeParser is its only direct implementation. Charles 4 had it as the
	COMMENT unnamed com.xk72.proxy.ssl.v, so the class name is a reading of the role.
	COMMENT The method names below come from the record content types SSLRecordParser switches on:
	COMMENT 20 change_cipher_spec, 21 alert, 22 handshake, 23 application_data.
	METHOD method_3792 handshakeSizeChanged (J)V
		COMMENT the running total of change_cipher_spec, alert and handshake record bytes seen so far,
		COMMENT reported after each such record.
		ARG 1 totalBytes
	METHOD method_3793 handshakeRecord ([B)V
		COMMENT the reassembled body of a content-type 22 record.
		ARG 1 body
	METHOD method_3174 alert (BB)V
		COMMENT a content-type 21 record; the subclasses treat level 2 as fatal and record the
		COMMENT description on the ProxyEvent.
		ARG 1 level
		ARG 2 description
	METHOD method_3747 changeCipherSpec ()V
	METHOD method_3745 applicationData ()V
	METHOD method_3750 encryptedRecord ()V
		COMMENT an alert or handshake record arriving after change_cipher_spec, so its body cannot be
		COMMENT parsed.
	METHOD method_3749 unknownRecord ()V
		COMMENT a record whose content type is none of the four known ones.
	METHOD method_3746 notSslRecord ()V
		COMMENT the five header bytes did not pass SSLRecordParser's plausibility check, so the stream
		COMMENT is not TLS at all.
